Sample rate Max is 500k Samples/Second but split between 3 channels
Resolution 24 bits
Max Distance "Not sure yet"

The idea is:

Program #1 Signal Generator
Generate 3 seperate wave forms
|xu[n]|+|yu[n]|+|zu[n]| = h[n], where xu[n] = x[n]/(|<x,y,z>|)  0 <= h[n] <= 3

Generate code to vary signals at some expected rate
Vary amplitude, 0 - 2^12. 2^12 bias so, 2^12 represents 0V
Vary frequency, Max signal frequency is 1Khz, 

Generate a copy of the signal but with noise added. This should be the one sent to the DSP and the original should be sent to the analysis
Sample each wave form at a frequency of 500k/3, alternate T_s time between x, y, z to match ADC
Send data through socket to signal processor program to simulate SPI
Send data through socket to analysis program

Program #2 Real SPI management version
Basically just packages SPI values into a vector for the DSP program
Configures the SPI interfaces

Program #3 DSP
Recieve 3 packages of 24 bytes
Filter

Program #4 Transmit Handling,
Recieve information about frequency selection and transmit it to the DSP program

Program #5 Anaylsis
Recieve the original signal, (noisy signal?), and dsp signal.
Perform various analysis to determine the effectiveness of the dsp program













